              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this is the BEST sauce ever!! We've been to Aruba, Mexico, Costa Rica and Argentina in some of the best Argentinan restaurants and this is the best representative of the chimichurri sauce"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "C Forhan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great recipe with some additions, make sure to use Italian parsley. Double the lemon juice and add the same amount of cilantro as parsley. I also added 2 tablespoons of red wine vinegar. This is exactly the chimmichuri sauce you get at the Brazilian BBQ restaurants.",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-08T20:39:51.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "markgugs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Agree with one of the reviews below, this is badly lacking in acidity, I'd suggest doubling the lemon juice and/or adding a tbsp. of white wine vinegar, or white balsamic vinegar. Otherwise the fresh herbs dominate everything else.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-24T15:28:17.420Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Souix Chef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't have parsley but I did have two bunches of cilantro so I gave it a shot and OMG, the very best sauce on fish, chicken and steak! \n**UPDATE** I mixed a quarter cup of this in with two cups of alfredo sauce and put it on pasta, very delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-01T10:20:48.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SZYQ1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe exactly as written and it was very good. I thought it would be good to put everything in my little chopper for a couple of pulses and it blended a little too much, which is my fault. While I liked this chimichurri, I felt it could use a tad more acid and I opted to splash in a tiny bit of red wine vinegar. Just my personal preference I suppose. Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2019-08-16T14:48:27.090Z"
          },
          {
